export anchor TestFix:
    description:
        A failure also asks the tool for a fix: the instructions an agent
        needs to make the statement true, in ASD-STE100 like the explanation,
        written as commands, naming each file to change and what to change in
        it. The fix aims at what the test examines. Against spec it changes
        the specification, in its .pi source, and not the code. Against code
        it changes the code, and not the specification. Against both it gives
        the changes to each as two parts, a part only for a side that doesn't
        make the statement true, so that afterwards the two agree. It is asked
        for in the same session as the verdict, so it costs no extra run.
